{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.798Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Both the task's verify (`node --import tsx --import ./tests/git-test-env.ts --test tests/mcp-tools.test.ts`) and the proposal's verify (`pnpm verify`) pass green.\n\n## Summary\n\n**`src/cli/mcp-tools.ts`** (240 lines) implements cli-foundation \"MCP planning tools\":\n- Exports the `McpTarget` type (`{ kind: 'local', cwd }` / `{ kind: 'remote', server, home? }`) and `createMcpTools(target)`, returning exactly the nine tools in table order — `plan`, the five file tools, `spec`, `query`, `lint` — each with a one-line description and a JSON Schema `inputSchema` (string arguments, required where not optional, `additionalProperties: false`).\n- File tools delegate to `mcp-files.ts`, with a remote `workRoot` of `remoteWorkRoot(server, home)`.\n- Command tools send `{ command, args, options: {} }` with missing arguments as null. Locally they run through `createForwardedRunner(cwd)` (so `plan` keeps its no-brief refusal); against a server, `plan` → `planOnServer`, `lint` → `lintOnServer`, `spec`/`query` → `runOnServer`, with a thrown `CommandError` read as exit code, message and next step.\n- Tool text is every stdout/stderr chunk in arrival order plus the error and `Next:` lines exactly as `runCli` prints them; `isError` is true exactly when the exit code is non-zero.\n- `createMcpTools` carries the four `@scenario cli-foundation:` tags and `@adr 014`.\n\n**`tests/mcp-tools.test.ts`** covers \"Tools give the CLI's text\" (all three rows against the command functions' string writers), \"Plan prepares the prompt\" via `formatNextStep(readNextStep(...))`, \"No tap tools\", and \"Planning against a server\" (real `startWebServer` with a site and `createForwardedRunner`, temporary home, server closed in an `after` hook — plan fills the working copy, `write_file` writes there, and after `lint` the server folder holds `tasks/2.md` with the server's lint text).\n\nNo preexisting files were changed; the full suite, typecheck, build and lint all pass."}}
