{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-10T00:48:45.739Z","data":{"text":"Done. Task 3 is complete.\n\n**Summary**\n\nAdded `src/cli/mcp-tools.ts` implementing cli-foundation \"MCP planning tools\":\n- Exports `McpTarget` and `createMcpTools(target)`, returning exactly the nine tools in spec order (`plan`, `list_files`, `read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `delete_file`, `spec`, `query`, `lint`) with one-line descriptions and JSON Schemas (`additionalProperties: false`, required args listed).\n- File tools delegate to `mcp-files.ts`, using a remote source with `workRoot = remoteWorkRoot(server, home)`.\n- Locally command tools run through `createForwardedRunner(cwd)`; against a server `plan`/`lint` use `planOnServer`/`lintOnServer` and `spec`/`query` use `runOnServer`. Text mirrors `runCli` (chunks in arrival order, then error line, then `Next:`), and `isError` tracks the exit code.\n- Tagged with the four `@scenario cli-foundation:` lines and `@adr 014`.\n\nAdded `tests/mcp-tools.test.ts` covering the tool list, CLI-text parity for `spec`/`query`/`lint`, the plan handoff against `formatNextStep(readNextStep(...))`, the no-brief refusal, and a full plan→write→lint round trip against a real `startWebServer` (closed in `after`).\n\n`pnpm verify` passes: 3706 main tests + 152 UI tests, 0 failures, lint clean. Result written to `openspec/changes/163-local-mcp/.run/results/3.md`."}}
